SUMMARY OF MASTER BANDWIDTH PURCHASE AND SALE AGREEMENT


Set forth below is a summary of certain provisions of the Master Bandwidth Purchase and Sale Agreement (the “Master Agreement”).  All capitalized terms used herein shall have the meaning set forth in the Master Agreement.


Scope of Agreement.  The Master Agreement is a bilateral document for the purchase and sale of Bandwidth Units.  The contracting parties may select the Bandwidth Units and Quality of Service specified in one of the nine attached annexes, or may customize the particular transaction in the Confirmation.  Each Transaction is for a one month term, which may not necessarily correspond to a calendar month.  Quality of Services is defined in terms of Errored Seconds, Severely Errored Seconds and Unavailable Seconds.


Transaction Procedures.  Transactions may occur verbally, electronically or pursuant to a Transaction Agreement.  ________________ will send a written confirmation of a Transaction within three days of the Trade Date.  A Transaction is not invalidated by ___________________’s failure to send a Confirmation.  (A Transaction Agreement will be deemed to be a Confirmation.)


Confirmations.  Confirmations must be executed or objected to within three days of receipt.  Failure to respond will be deemed to be acceptance of the Confirmation.


Demarcation Point.  The Demarcation Point and any other required information shall be exchanged in accordance with the timeframe specified in the Confirmation.  Seller shall provide such information in advance of Buyer.  If either party fails to provide the necessary information, such party will be liable for monetary damages. 

Term of the Master Agreement.  The Master Agreement is evergreen but may be terminated by either party on 30 days prior written notice.


Default Interest Rate.  The default interest rate is equal to the prime commercial lending rate, as published in the Wall Street Journal, plus two percent per annum.

7. Damages:


If Seller fails to deliver at start of Month, damages shall equal (Days of failure/30) x (Cover Price (if positive) + Contract Price (to the extent paid by Buyer)).
If Buyer fails to accept, damages shall equal the Contract Price, i.e., take or pay.
If Seller fails to provide QoS Bandwidth, damages shall be as specified in Annex or Confirmation. (Note, QoS failures may be severe enough to constitute an Event of Default Triggering Event, as specified in Annex or Confirmation.)

Buyer must give Seller notice of noncompliance within two Business Days of the occurrence of such noncompliance or Buyer’s right to above damages are waived.


Local Access Service Charges. Local Access Service charges are the sole responsibility of the Buyer.


Upgrade of Pooling Point.  Either party may request an upgrade, modification or addition to a Pooling Point on seven days prior written notice.  For an Upgrade to occur, the other Party must consent or fail to object within seven days of delivery of the request.  If a party objects to an Upgrade within the seven-day period, no Upgrade may occur.


Billing.  Seller will invoice Buyer on or before the first Day of the month.  Buyer will be billed in advance for Bandwidth Units.  Only the first invoice will include any prior period.  Payments must be made by wire transfer on or before the 25th day of the month.  Netting and setoff is permitted.



11. Events of Default.


Nonpayment
Failure to comply with obligations under the Agreement
Bankruptcy of a Party
Failure of a Guarantor
Breach of a representation or warranty
Occurrence of an Event of Default Triggering Event (i.e., QoS)
Default by a Party or a guarantor on indebtedness to third parties
Material Adverse Change

12. Cure Period for Certain Defaults.


Payment defaults must be cured within three Business Days after written notice.
Nonpayment defaults must be cured within five Business Days after written notice.


Remedies for Defaults.


Declare an Early Termination Date (requires 20 days notice) and collect any owing Early Termination Payment. The Early Termination Payment is calculated by comparing the value of each terminated transaction to the market value of an equivalent replacement transaction.
Withhold payments until the Event of Default is cured.
Suspend performance until the Event of Default is cured.
Terminate all Transactions if the default is a payment default or a Default Triggering Event has occurred.


Credit Enhancement.  Bracketed language is provided for guaranties and performance assurance requirements.  The Credit Department will determine whether such provisions are appropriate for a particular counterparty.


Force Majeure.


Either party or the Pooling Point Administrator (in connection with the pooling point or related facilities) may declare an event of Force Majeure.
To qualify as an event of Force Majeure, the following conditions must exist:
  

The event must not be in the reasonable control of the party claiming suspension, and
The event must prevent the performance not only of the claiming party, but also prevent the performance of “similarly situated third parties” involved in the market for bandwidth.

c.  The following does not constitute an event of force majeure:


Economic hardship by either party.
Mechanical or equipment failure.
Any change in law or regulation after the Trade Date of the affected Transaction unless such change prevents performance by all similarly situated parties.


Taxes.   Buyer is responsible for all Taxes applicable to the Transaction.  Buyer is entitled to declare an Early Termination Date if a material New Tax is enacted and it is not subject to “pass through” reimbursement by another third party.  Buyer must give the Seller at least 30 days prior written notice of its intent to declare an Early Termination Date.


Limited Liability for Damages.  Only direct, actual damages are recoverable.  Neither party shall be liable for consequential, incidental, punitive or exemplary damages.


Representations and Warranties. Each party makes standard representations and warranties concerning organization, execution, enforceability, etc.


Arbitration.  Disputes under the Master Agreement will be resolved by binding arbitration in accordance with the Commercial Arbitration Rules of the American Arbitration Association.


Assignment.  A party may assign its rights under the Master Agreement under the following circumstances:


The other party consents,
Assignment is to an Affiliate and there is no degradation of creditworthiness, or
Assignment is incident to a merger or reorganization.


Notices.  Notices must be in writing and may be given by hand, facsimile, overnight mail or courier.


Governing Law.  The laws of the State of New York govern the Master Agreement.


Indemnity.


Each party will indemnify the other for Claims for property damage, personal injury or death caused by such party’s negligence or willful misconduct.
Buyer will indemnify Seller for any claims by third parties resulting from any defect in or failure to provide Bandwidth Units sold under the Master Agreement.


MASTER BANDWIDTH PURCHASE AND SALE AGREEMENT

This Master Bandwidth Purchase and Sale Agreement, together with any amendment, modification or change made in accordance with Section 12.6 hereof (this “Master Agreement”) is entered into as of ___________________ (“Effective Date”) between _____________________________, a [corporation][partnership] organized under the laws of the State of [   ] (“Counterparty”) and _____________________, a [corporation][partnership] organized under the laws of the State of [__________________] (“Company”).   Company and Counterparty shall each be referred to as a “Party” under this Master Agreement.  Counterparty and Company hereby agree as follows:
1. Agreement for Transactions.
1.1.  Scope of Agreement.  From time to time, the Parties may, but shall not be obligated to, enter into binding Transactions for the purchase or sale of Bandwidth Units, as hereinafter defined.  Each Transaction shall be effectuated, evidenced and governed in accordance with this Master Agreement and the documents and other confirming evidence, whether a Transaction Agreement (as defined below) or any other form of Confirmation (as defined below).  All Transactions are entered into in reliance on the fact that this Master Agreement and all Confirmations form a single agreement between the Parties (collectively referred to as this “Agreement”) and the Parties would not otherwise enter into any Transactions.  Each Confirmation shall supplement and form a part of, and be subject to, this Master Agreement and shall be read and construed together with this Master Agreement.  Any capitalized term used herein and not defined in the Section in which it appears shall have the meaning set forth in Section 2 hereof.
1.2.  Transaction Procedures.  It is the intent of the Parties to facilitate Transactions in accordance with the procedures set forth in this Section 1 and to assure that such Transactions are valid and enforceable for the mutual benefit of the Parties.  Any Transaction may be formed and effectuated and shall be legally binding (a) by a telephone conversation that may be recorded (each Party thereby and hereby consenting to the recording of its representatives’ telephone conversations without any further notice) or any exchange of retrievable electronic communications between the Parties or their respective representatives whereby an offer and acceptance shall constitute the agreement of the Parties to a Transaction, or (b) if, and only if, the Parties have previously stipulated by a written agreement executed by both Parties, by a written Transaction Agreement executed by the Parties (including by facsimile and/or counterparts).  As a material part of the consideration for entering into a Transaction, each Party hereby waives and agrees not to contest or assert any defense to (i) the validity or enforceability of Transactions under laws relating to whether certain agreements are to be in writing or signed by such Party to be thereby bound, or (ii) the authority of any employee or representative of such Party to enter into a Transaction.  Subject to the applicable rules of evidence, all telephone recordings and retrievals of computer or other electronic messages may be offered into evidence and used to prove the existence of oral agreements as to Transactions between the Parties, but it is understood that such tangible documentation need not reference all of the terms of the Transaction, that it is not the sole evidence of such terms, and that, in the event of a conflict between the tangible documentation of the oral agreement and the subsequent accepted Confirmation, as provided for in Section 1.3, the Confirmation shall prevail.  Any Transaction formed between the Parties pursuant to the procedures set forth in this Section 1 shall be considered to be a “writing” or “in writing” and to have been “signed” by the Parties, and any tape recording of a Transaction and/or retrieval of any computer or other electronic message forming a Transaction shall be considered to constitute an “original” document evidencing the Transaction.
1.3.  Confirmations.  The Parties agree that Company may confirm a Transaction entered into pursuant to the provisions of Section 1.2(a) above by giving to Counterparty, within three (3) Business Days after the Trade Date, a written or electronic notice (“Confirmation”) confirming the specific terms (other than those terms described in Section 1.4 below) of such Transaction.  Such Confirmation shall be substantially in the form of Exhibit A hereto (or in such other form as the Parties may agree), provided, however, that Company’s failure to send such Confirmation or to send such Confirmation within such three (3) Business Day period shall not invalidate any Transaction previously entered into in accordance with Section 1.2.  If a Confirmation is not executed by Counterparty (with any objections to the accuracy of the contents noted thereon) and returned to Company (or is not otherwise objected to by written notice to Company) within three (3) Business Days after Counterparty’s receipt thereof, such Confirmation will be deemed correct as given and shall constitute conclusive and binding evidence of such Transaction and the final expression of the terms thereof.  Except as otherwise provided in this Agreement, in the event of any irreconcilable, express conflict between the provisions of this Agreement and the provisions of any Confirmation, the terms of such Confirmation will control for the relevant Transaction.
1.4.  Exchange of Demarcation Point and Other Information.  Within the time period set forth in the Confirmation applicable to a Transaction (or if no time period is set forth in a Confirmation, 60 Days prior to the beginning of the Term), the Parties agree to exchange and provide to the Pooling Point Administrator, the Demarcation Point and any other information required by the Pooling Point Administrator (including all other operational data that may be required for the Pooling Point Administrator to schedule and test the Bandwidth Unit(s)).  Seller shall provide such Demarcation Point and other information to Buyer and the Pooling Point Administrator in advance of Buyer.  In the event that Seller fails to so provide such Demarcation Point or other information (or causes or prevents the Buyer from providing such Demarcation Point or other information), such event shall constitute a failure of Seller under Section 3.3(a)(i) hereof and Buyer shall be entitled to the applicable remedies in respect thereof.  In the event that Buyer fails to provide such Demarcation Point or other information, such event shall constitute a failure of Buyer under Section 3.3(a)(ii) hereof and Seller shall be entitled to the applicable remedies in respect thereof.  An event giving rise to any payment obligation under this Section 1.4 or Section 3.3 shall not constitute an “Event of Default” to the extent that such payment obligation is satisfied on a timely basis.
1.5. Term of Master Agreement.  This Master Agreement shall be effective as of the Effective Date and shall remain in effect until terminated by either Party upon 30 days prior written notice to the other Party; provided, however, that this Master Agreement shall remain in effect with respect to any Transaction(s) entered into prior to the effective date of such termination until both Parties have fulfilled all their respective obligations with respect thereto.
