6. Events of Default and Remedies.
6.1.  Events of Default.  An event of default (an “Event of Default”) with respect to a Party (the “Defaulting Party”) shall mean any of the following:
(a) the failure of the Defaulting Party to pay any amount when due under this Agreement, if such failure is not remedied within three (3) Business Days after written notice thereof;
(b) the failure of the Defaulting Party to comply with any of its obligations under this Agreement (other than defaults that are otherwise specifically set forth in this Section 6.1, the failure to provide or accept Bandwidth Unit(s) or failures that constitute QoS Damage Triggering Events, remedies for the latter two of which are provided in Section 3.3(a) and Section 3.3(b), respectively), and such failure is not excused by Force Majeure or cured within five (5) Business Days after written notice thereof to the Defaulting Party;
(c) the Defaulting Party shall be subject to a Bankruptcy Proceeding;
