DS-3
STS-1

The following benchmark quality of service standards (“BQoS”) are applicable to DS-3 Bandwidth Units:

Not more than 5 Errored Seconds/Day.
Not more than 10 Severely Errored Seconds/Day.
Not more than 60 Unavailable Seconds/Month.

“DS-3” means digital signal, level 3, which is a 44.736 Mbps digital line section passing between two system interface points, together with the interconnection interfaces pertaining thereto in accordance with American National Standards Institute (ANSI) T1.102-1993. 
“Mbps” means million bits per second.


QoS Damage Triggering Event
BQoS Damages
In any Day Errored Seconds exceed 5
1/720 of the sum of (A) the Cover Price of the affected Bandwidth Unit, and (B) the Contract Price of the affected Bandwidth Unit
In any Day Severely Errored Seconds exceed 10
1/720 of the sum of (A) the Cover Price of the affected Bandwidth Unit, and (B) the Contract Price of the affected Bandwidth Unit
In any Month Unavailable Seconds equal 61 up to 3,600
1/720 of the sum of (A) the Cover Price of the affected Bandwidth Unit, and (B) the Contract Price of the affected Bandwidth Unit
In any Month Unavailable Seconds exceed 3,600
1/720 of the product of (i) the sum of (A) the Cover Price of the affected Bandwidth Unit, and (B) the Contract Price of the affected Bandwidth Unit, and (ii) (A) the total number of Unavailable Seconds in such Month, divided by (B) 3,600 (rounded up to the next whole number)


Event of Default Triggering Event
In any Month Errored Seconds exceed 40 on 10 or more Days
In any Month Severely Errored Seconds exceed 40 on 10 or more Days
In any Month Unavailable Seconds equal or exceed 604,800

